//@version=5
indicator("UCTPROBE_VW_OBJECT_GC_A", overlay = false)

// ─── 2026-09-28 — OBJECT-LANE TRIAGE C7, PROBE A OF 4: THE CORPUS SPLIT, REPRODUCED
//
// `docs/pine/vendor-harness/objects-triage-2026-09-28.md` § C7. TradingView keeps
// the NEWEST n objects by id (FIFO holds — measured), but n itself fits no rule:
//
//   script (corpus/committed/)   shape                                     cap  held
//   contraction-box  (v5)        box.new at GLOBAL scope, EVERY bar,        50   50
//                                coordinates na on most bars
//   makuchaku FVG    (v4)        box.new inside `if`, SPORADIC, real        50   51
//                                coordinates, one created on the last bar
//   ultimate-pivot   (v5)        inside `if`, ~every bar, 9 lines + 9       50   51/51
//                                labels per bar (labels unheld, real y)
//   multi-tf S&D     (v5)        504 box.new(na,…) in ONE bar (isfirst,     500  504
//                                for-loop, pushed into arrays), none after
//
// THE COMPETING RULES (the same letters in probes A–D):
//   H1 STRICT        a create at the cap evicts the oldest first: live ≤ cap always
//                    (OURS TODAY — `objectRuntime` evicts on create)
//   H2 TRIM-THEN-ADD a create trims to cap THEN adds: cap+1 after any create
//   H3 BAR-END       one trim pass when a bar finishes. H3a: the last bar's pass runs
//                    (final = cap); H3b: it runs at the NEXT bar's start, so the final
//                    bar keeps its creates (final = cap + creates on the last bar)
//   H4 SPARE-THIS-BAR a trim never takes an object created on the trimming bar
//   H5 SCOPE         global-scope creates are collected to cap, creates inside a local
//                    block (`if`) keep one more — the only dimension that splits
//                    contraction-box (50) from BOTH makuchaku and ultimate (51)
//   H6 RATE          sporadic creation keeps one more than every-bar creation
//   H7 NA-COORD      objects with na coordinates are counted/collected differently
//   (H8 live-vs-ring and H9 var-exempt: probe C. H10 lazy/batched GC: probe D.)
//
// THIS PROBE reproduces the three one-per-call shapes at the CORPUS'S OWN CAP
// (default ≈ 50 — no max_*_count, exactly like the three scripts). If it does NOT
// read 50 / 51 / 51, the split is not a shape effect and probe B's pairwise reading
// is moot; say so before grading B.
//
//   O1  boxes  "AB <bar>"   CONTRACTION shape — global scope, every bar, coordinates
//                            na unless bar_index % 5 == 0
//   O2  labels "AL <bar>"   MAKUCHAKU shape — inside `if`, on bar_index % 4 == 0 OR
//                            the last bar (makuchaku created on its last bar), real
//   O3  lines  (no text)    ULTIMATE shape — inside `if`, every bar, 3 per bar,
//                            width = 1, 2, 3 in call order, unheld
//
//   held at the end    H1   H2   H3a  H3b  H4   H5   H6   H7
//   O1 boxes           50   51   50   51   50   50   50   ≠O1 of B
//   O2 labels          50   51   50   51   50   51   51   —
//   O3 lines           50   51   50   53   50   51   50   —
//   (the corpus says: 50 / 51 / 51)
//
// ⭐ READ BY ID, NOT BY COUNT ALONE. One monotonic id counter serves all families.
// Per bar the calls run in THIS order: box (1 id), label (0 or 1), line w1, w2, w3
// — so bar b's box id is the anchor, and every other id on b follows it. A held
// set must be the newest n by id; a gap inside it is itself a finding. Box and
// label text carry the bar; a line's bar is its id's position after that anchor.
// The capture records `id`, `t` (text) and `w` (width); x/y are the vendor's own
// indices, NOT bar_index — never read the bar off a coordinate.
//
//   A00  bar_index                       CONTROL
//   A01  barstate.isconfirmed ? 1 : 0    last bar 0 = captured while FORMING (the
//                                        corpus was read after the close: forming=false)
//   A02  barstate.islast ? 1 : 0         marks the bar every "last bar" rule means
//   A03  O2 created on this bar ? 1 : 0  the makuchaku condition, per bar
//
// ⛔ CAPTURE TWICE, inputs at defaults (none), AFTER THE CLOSE (the corpus's
// condition): AMEX:SPY 1D (whatever history loads — only the end state is read)
// and AMEX:SPY W (a different last bar, so a different bar_index % 4 phase).
//
// ours today (2026-09-28, `runOurSide` at d24d526e2 on the NYSE:RDDT 1D fixture's
// 632 bars): TRANSLATES clean — 4 plots, 5 object ops, 0 drops. Holds 50 / 50 / 50
// (H1): boxes AB 582..631 (40 of them undrawable, na coordinates — counted as
// held), labels AL 436..628 by 4s + AL 631, lines 50.

plot(bar_index, "A00_bar_index_CONTROL")
plot(barstate.isconfirmed ? 1 : 0, "A01_isconfirmed")
plot(barstate.islast ? 1 : 0, "A02_islast")

// O1 — contraction-box shape: global scope, every bar, na coordinates on most bars
realAB = bar_index % 5 == 0
box.new(realAB ? bar_index : na, realAB ? 1.0 : na, realAB ? bar_index + 1 : na, realAB ? 0.0 : na, text = "AB " + str.tostring(bar_index))

// O2 — makuchaku shape: inside `if`, sporadic, and always on the last bar
makeAL = bar_index % 4 == 0 or barstate.islast
if makeAL
    label.new(bar_index, 1.0, "AL " + str.tostring(bar_index))
plot(makeAL ? 1 : 0, "A03_O2_created_this_bar")

// O3 — ultimate-pivot shape: inside `if` (a condition the compiler cannot fold;
// true on every SPY bar), several per bar, unheld
if close > 0
    line.new(bar_index, 1.0, bar_index + 1, 1.0, width = 1)
    line.new(bar_index, 2.0, bar_index + 1, 2.0, width = 2)
    line.new(bar_index, 3.0, bar_index + 1, 3.0, width = 3)
